## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to map a real-world beginner task into Azure services with clear data flow, tenant isolation, and DR basics.

## Key Concepts

- Event Grid triggering from blob events
- Tenant isolation in Cosmos DB partition keys
- Blob Storage design per-tenant namespaces
- Functions for image processing; API Management for surface
- Basic DR: GRS/Multi-region, Cosmos multi-region
- BYOK via Key Vault and managed identities
- Cost control: autoscale, monitoring, and budgets

## Code Example

```javascript
// Sample Function skeleton that handles BlobCreated event
module.exports = async function(context, eventGridEvent) {
  const blobUrl = eventGridEvent.data.url;
  context.log('Detected blob:', blobUrl);
  // enqueue thumbnail task (placeholder)
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test per-tenant isolation guarantees in this design?
- What changes would you make to support millions of tenants and higher throughput?

